<%- include("partials/head") %>
<%- include("partials/header") %>
<%- include("partials/nav") %>

<main class="resume-layout">
  <%- include("partials/contactModal") %>

  <article class="project-detail">
    <header class="card project-detail-hero">
      <a href="/projects" class="project-back-link">Back to projects</a>
      <p class="project-tag">Browser Game · Vanilla JavaScript / JSON / CSS</p>
      <h1>Speed Dungeon</h1>
      <p>
        A static browser game where the player clears short dungeon rooms,
        collects Power Points and uses that progress in a final boss fight.
        The project focuses on game-state logic, age-based content, room
        transitions, timers, assets and mobile controls.
      </p>

      <div class="project-detail-actions">
        <a
          href="https://speed-dungeon.onrender.com"
          class="project-link project-link-primary"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          Live Demo
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/STU6266/speed-dungeon"
          class="project-link project-link-secondary"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="project-detail-media-grid" aria-label="Speed Dungeon visuals">
      <figure class="project-media-card">
        <img
          src="/images/projects/speed-dungeon/start-screen.png"
          alt="Speed Dungeon start screen with age group selection and run stats"
          width="1440"
          height="1000"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>Start screen with age group selection</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="project-media-card">
        <img
          src="/images/projects/speed-dungeon/corridor-run.png"
          alt="Speed Dungeon corridor room showing the player dodging dungeon walls during a timed run"
          width="1440"
          height="1000"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>Active corridor room during a timed run</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="project-media-card project-media-card--portrait">
        <img
          src="/images/projects/speed-dungeon/mobile-controls.png"
          alt="Mobile Speed Dungeon corridor room with touch controls for moving left and right"
          width="390"
          height="1000"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>Mobile touch controls for keyboard-style input</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="project-detail-grid">
      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
          Speed Dungeon is a small arcade-style dungeon run. The player starts a
          three-minute run, clears room challenges, earns Power Points and then
          faces a boss where the collected power affects the final fight.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>Tech Stack</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>HTML, CSS and vanilla JavaScript</li>
          <li>JSON files for riddle and image-search room content</li>
          <li>WebP assets for room backgrounds and picture-based rooms</li>
          <li>Static Render deployment with a build step into <code>dist/</code></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>Game Systems</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Age groups: 0-7, 8-11, 12-15 and 16+</li>
          <li>Room types: corridor, reaction fight, math lock, image search and riddle</li>
          <li>Global run state for timer, cleared rooms and Power Points</li>
          <li>Final boss fight with dodge keys and attack timing</li>
          <li>Mobile touch controls for rooms that normally use keyboard input</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>Architecture</h2>
        <p>
          The game is served as a static site. <code>index.html</code> provides
          the game shell, HUD, room containers and mobile controls. The main
          JavaScript file owns room transitions, timers, input handling, state
          updates and JSON data loading. CSS is split into focused files for
          layout, room types, boss fight and mobile controls.
        </p>
        <ol class="engineering-flow" aria-label="Speed Dungeon engineering flow">
          <li>Start and age selection</li>
          <li>Room engine</li>
          <li>JSON content and assets</li>
          <li>Player input/mobile controls</li>
          <li>Timer and boss flow</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>Challenges</h2>
        <p>
          The difficult part was making several different mini-games behave like
          one connected run. The timer, room completion, mistakes, power gain,
          mobile input and boss transition all need to work together without a
          backend or framework managing state for me.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>Still WIP</h2>
        <p>
          This version is playable, but not finished as a polished game. The
          main JavaScript file is still intentionally kept in one file to avoid
          changing behavior during cleanup. Future work would be splitting room
          logic into modules, adding more content/assets and expanding room
          coverage for the youngest age group.
        </p>
      </section>
    </section>
  </article>
</main>

<%- include("partials/footer") %>
